IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc4-part5-assessment`
IMPORT `uc4-part8-ch1-no-requirements`

-- Tests of uc4-part8-ch1-no-requirements.l4: regulation 99.
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside the assertion.
-- The date asked about is 1 June 2026 unless a case says otherwise.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Fixtures.
GIVEN court IS A BOOLEAN
      tribunal IS A BOOLEAN
      listed IS A BOOLEAN
      party IS A BOOLEAN
      witness IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Attendance at a court or tribunal`
`test — attendance` court tribunal listed party witness MEANS `Attendance at a court or tribunal` WITH
    `the claimant is attending a court` IS court
    `the claimant is attending a tribunal` IS tribunal
    `the tribunal is listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992` IS listed
    `the claimant is attending as a party to any proceedings` IS party
    `the claimant is attending as a witness` IS witness

GIVEN pending IS A BOOLEAN
      sentence IS A BOOLEAN
      release IS A BOOLEAN
      hospital IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Detention
`test — detention` pending sentence release hospital MEANS Detention WITH
    `detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction` IS pending
    `detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court` IS sentence
    `on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989` IS release
    `detained in hospital under the mental health Acts` IS hospital

GIVEN partner IS A MAYBE DATE
      child IS A MAYBE DATE
      parent IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Deaths within the past 6 months`
`test — deaths` partner child parent MEANS `Deaths within the past 6 months` WITH
    `date of death of the other member of the couple, where the claimant was a member of a couple` IS partner
    `date of death of a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant or, where the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member, was responsible` IS child
    `date of death of a child, where the claimant was the child's parent` IS parent

GIVEN days IS A NUMBER
      periods IS A NUMBER
      declaration IS A BOOLEAN
      further IS A BOOLEAN
      requested IS A BOOLEAN
      statement IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Unfitness for work facts`
`test — unfit` days periods declaration further requested statement MEANS `Unfitness for work facts` WITH
    `days for which the claimant is unfit for work after the date that the evidence referred to in sub-paragraph (b) is provided` IS days
    `number of such periods of unfitness for work in the period of 12 months, including this one` IS periods
    `the claimant has provided a declaration, in such manner and form as the Secretary of State approves, that the claimant is unfit for work` IS declaration
    `the claimant is unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days` IS further
    `the Secretary of State has requested a statement for those further days` IS requested
    `the claimant has provided a statement given in accordance with the rules set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work` IS statement

-- Seven days of unfitness, the first period in the year, the declaration given, no further days.
`test — a short absence` MEANS `test — unfit` 7 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN noLcw IS A BOOLEAN
      severe IS A BOOLEAN
      lcw IS A BOOLEAN
      notSevere IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Previous determinations`
`test — previous` noLcw severe lcw notSevere MEANS `Previous determinations` WITH
    `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant does not have limited capability for work` IS noLcw
    `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS severe
    `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant has limited capability for work` IS lcw
    `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS notSevere

GIVEN eventDate IS A DATE
      carer IS A BOOLEAN
      previousCarer IS A BOOLEAN
      parentDied IS A BOOLEAN
      sibling IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
      commercial IS A BOOLEAN
      victim IS A BOOLEAN
      perpetrator IS A BOOLEAN
      disruption IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Event affecting a child in the claimant's care`
`test — event` eventDate carer previousCarer parentDied sibling other commercial victim perpetrator disruption MEANS `Event affecting a child in the claimant's care` WITH
    `date of the event` IS eventDate
    `the claimant is the responsible carer of a child` IS carer
    `a person who was previously the responsible carer of that child has died` IS previousCarer
    `a parent of that child has died` IS parentDied
    `a brother or sister of that child has died` IS sibling
    `any other person who, at the time of their death, normally lived in the same accommodation as that child has died` IS other
    `that other person was liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of that accommodation` IS commercial
    `the child has been the victim of, or witness to, an incident of violence or abuse` IS victim
    `the claimant is the perpetrator of that violence or abuse` IS perpetrator
    `the event has resulted in significant disruption to the claimant's normal childcare responsibilities` IS disruption

-- A parent died on 1 June 2025; the claimant is the responsible carer; the event disrupted childcare.
`test — a parent died` MEANS `test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph (7).
#ASSERT `reg 99(7) — the body is a tribunal` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(7) — the body is a tribunal` FALSE)

-- Paragraph (3)(a): a court, or a tribunal listed in Schedule 1, and a party or a witness.
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(a) — the claimant is attending a court or tribunal as a party or as a witness` (`test — attendance` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(a) — the claimant is attending a court or tribunal as a party or as a witness` (`test — attendance` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(a) — the claimant is attending a court or tribunal as a party or as a witness` (`test — attendance` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(a) — the claimant is attending a court or tribunal as a party or as a witness` (`test — attendance` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- A body that is not listed is not a tribunal for this regulation.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(a) — the claimant is attending a court or tribunal as a party or as a witness` (`test — attendance` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- Attending only as an observer is neither party nor witness.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(a) — the claimant is attending a court or tribunal as a party or as a witness` (`test — attendance` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(a) — the claimant is attending a court or tribunal as a party or as a witness` (`test — attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))

-- Paragraph (3)(b): a prisoner, by the core's definition of regulation 2.
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(b) — the claimant is a prisoner` (`test — detention` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(b) — the claimant is a prisoner` (`test — detention` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(b) — the claimant is a prisoner` (`test — detention` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Detained in hospital under the mental health Acts is not a prisoner.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(b) — the claimant is a prisoner` (`test — detention` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(b) — the claimant is a prisoner` (`test — detention` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

-- Paragraph (3)(c).
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(c) — regulation 11(3) applies to the claimant` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(c) — regulation 11(3) applies to the claimant` FALSE)

-- Paragraph (3)(d): a death on 2 December 2025 is within the past 6 months of 1 June 2026 (the 6 months end on 1 June 2026).
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(d) — a death on this date is within the past 6 months` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 2)) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
-- A death on 1 December 2025: 6 months have run out on 1 June 2026.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(d) — a death on this date is within the past 6 months` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1))
-- A death on the date asked about counts; a death in the future does not.
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(d) — a death on this date is within the past 6 months` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(d) — a death on this date is within the past 6 months` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 2)) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(d) — a death on this date is within the past 6 months` NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(d) — any of the following persons has died within the past 6 months` (`test — deaths` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(d) — any of the following persons has died within the past 6 months` (`test — deaths` NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)) NOTHING) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(d) — any of the following persons has died within the past 6 months` (`test — deaths` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1))) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(d) — any of the following persons has died within the past 6 months` (`test — deaths` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(d) — any of the following persons has died within the past 6 months` (`test — deaths` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1))) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1))

-- Paragraph (3)(e): in a course since 1 January 2026; "no more than 6 months" ends on 1 July 2026, inclusive.
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(e) — the claimant is in a course of treatment and has been for no more than 6 months` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(e) — the claimant is in a course of treatment and has been for no more than 6 months` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 2))
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(e) — the claimant is in a course of treatment and has been for no more than 6 months` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(e) — the claimant is in a course of treatment and has been for no more than 6 months` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(e) — the claimant is in a course of treatment and has been for no more than 6 months` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1))

-- Paragraph (3)(f): under protection arrangements since 1 April 2026; 3 months end on 1 July 2026, inclusive.
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(f) — the claimant is under protection arrangements and has been for no more than 3 months` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(f) — the claimant is under protection arrangements and has been for no more than 3 months` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 2))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(f) — the claimant is under protection arrangements and has been for no more than 3 months` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(f) — the claimant is under protection arrangements and has been for no more than 3 months` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31))

-- Paragraph (3)(g).
#ASSERT `reg 99(3)(g) — the claimant is engaged in an activity approved as being in the nature of a public duty` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3)(g) — the claimant is engaged in an activity approved as being in the nature of a public duty` FALSE)

-- Paragraph (3) as a whole: each limb alone is enough.
#ASSERT `reg 99(3) — this paragraph applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(3) — this paragraph applies` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(3) — this paragraph applies` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(3) — this paragraph applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(3) — this paragraph applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(3) — this paragraph applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(3) — this paragraph applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(3) — this paragraph applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph (4)(a): 1 to 14 days, no more than 2 periods in the 12 months.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4)(a) — the claimant is unfit for work for a period and number of periods within the limits` (`test — unfit` 14 2 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(4)(a) — the claimant is unfit for work for a period and number of periods within the limits` (`test — unfit` 1 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4)(a) — the claimant is unfit for work for a period and number of periods within the limits` (`test — unfit` 15 2 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4)(a) — the claimant is unfit for work for a period and number of periods within the limits` (`test — unfit` 14 3 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4)(a) — the claimant is unfit for work for a period and number of periods within the limits` (`test — unfit` 0 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

-- Paragraph (4)(b)(i) and (ii).
#ASSERT `reg 99(4)(b)(i) — the claimant has provided a declaration for the first 7 days` `test — a short absence`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4)(b)(i) — the claimant has provided a declaration for the first 7 days` (`test — unfit` 7 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- Further days, requested, statement given.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4)(b)(ii) — the evidence for any further days has been provided if requested` (`test — unfit` 10 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Further days, requested, no statement.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4)(b)(ii) — the evidence for any further days has been provided if requested` (`test — unfit` 10 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
-- Further days, not requested: nothing is needed.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4)(b)(ii) — the evidence for any further days has been provided if requested` (`test — unfit` 10 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- No further days: nothing is needed even if a request was recorded.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4)(b)(ii) — the evidence for any further days has been provided if requested` (`test — unfit` 5 1 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(4)(b) — the claimant provides the evidence` `test — a short absence`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4)(b) — the claimant provides the evidence` (`test — unfit` 10 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4)(b) — the claimant provides the evidence` (`test — unfit` 10 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))

-- Paragraph (4ZB)(a)(i), (a)(ii) and (b).
#ASSERT `reg 99(4ZB)(a)(i) — it has previously been determined that the claimant does not have limited capability for work` (`test — previous` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4ZB)(a)(i) — it has previously been determined that the claimant does not have limited capability for work` (`test — previous` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `reg 99(4ZB)(a)(ii) — the claimant has previously been treated as not having limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity` (JUST `whether the claimant has limited capability for work`)
#ASSERT `reg 99(4ZB)(a)(ii) — the claimant has previously been treated as not having limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity` (JUST `whether the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity`)
-- Treatment as to the severe conditions criteria is not named in paragraph (4ZB)(a)(ii).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4ZB)(a)(ii) — the claimant has previously been treated as not having limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity` (JUST `whether the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant`))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4ZB)(a)(ii) — the claimant has previously been treated as not having limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity` NOTHING)
#ASSERT `reg 99(4ZB) — this paragraph applies` (`test — previous` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) NOTHING TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 99(4ZB) — this paragraph applies` (`test — previous` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (JUST `whether the claimant has limited capability for work`) TRUE
-- The Secretary of State's opinion is needed.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4ZB) — this paragraph applies` (`test — previous` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) NOTHING FALSE)
-- No previous determination or treatment.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4ZB) — this paragraph applies` (`test — previous` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) NOTHING TRUE)

-- Paragraph (4ZA): where (4ZB) applies, paragraph (4) is open only on a decision under regulation 41(1)(b).
#ASSERT `reg 99(4ZA) — paragraph (4) is open to the claimant` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4ZA) — paragraph (4) is open to the claimant` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(4ZA) — paragraph (4) is open to the claimant` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(4ZA) — paragraph (4) is open to the claimant` FALSE TRUE

-- Paragraph (4) as a whole.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4) — this paragraph applies` `test — a short absence` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(4) — this paragraph applies` `test — a short absence` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4) — this paragraph applies` `test — a short absence` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4) — this paragraph applies` (`test — unfit` 15 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4) — this paragraph applies` (`test — unfit` 7 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph (4A)(a): the deaths.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4A)(a) — a person has died` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(4A)(a) — a person has died` `test — a parent died`
#ASSERT `reg 99(4A)(a) — a person has died` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Another person who lived in the accommodation, not on a commercial basis.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4A)(a) — a person has died` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- ... but one who was liable to pay on a commercial basis is excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4A)(a) — a person has died` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4A)(a) — a person has died` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))

-- Paragraph (4A)(b): the child a victim of or witness to violence or abuse, the claimant not the perpetrator.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4A)(b) — the child has been a victim of or witness to violence or abuse` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4A)(b) — the child has been a victim of or witness to violence or abuse` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4A)(b) — the child has been a victim of or witness to violence or abuse` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))

-- Paragraph (4A): event on 1 June 2025; the 24 months end on 31 May 2027.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4A) — the circumstances for a period of one month` `test — a parent died` (YearMonthDay 2027 5 31)
#ASSERT `reg 99(4A) — the circumstances for a period of one month` `test — a parent died` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4A) — the circumstances for a period of one month` `test — a parent died` (YearMonthDay 2027 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4A) — the circumstances for a period of one month` `test — a parent died` (YearMonthDay 2025 5 31))
-- A violence event also qualifies.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4A) — the circumstances for a period of one month` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)
-- Not the responsible carer; no disruption; no qualifying event.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4A) — the circumstances for a period of one month` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4A) — the circumstances for a period of one month` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4A) — the circumstances for a period of one month` (`test — event` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1))

-- Paragraph (4B): windows of 6 months after an event on 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — the number of the 6-month window after the event in which a day falls` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — the number of the 6-month window after the event in which a day falls` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — the number of the 6-month window after the event in which a day falls` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — the number of the 6-month window after the event in which a day falls` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — the number of the 6-month window after the event in which a day falls` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — the number of the 6-month window after the event in which a day falls` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 6 30) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — the number of the 6-month window after the event in which a day falls` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — the number of the 6-month window after the event in which a day falls` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 12 31) EQUALS 3
-- A first period, then a second in the same window (not allowed), then one in another window (allowed).
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — a period of one month beginning on this day is allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4B) — a period of one month beginning on this day is allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — a period of one month beginning on this day is allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4B) — a period of one month beginning on this day is allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 12 31) (LIST YearMonthDay 2027 8 1))
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — a period of one month beginning on this day is allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 12 31) (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, YearMonthDay 2026 8 1, YearMonthDay 2027 2 1)
-- Outside the four windows: before the event, or 24 months or more after it.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4B) — a period of one month beginning on this day is allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31) EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4B) — a period of one month beginning on this day is allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2028 1 1) EMPTY)
#ASSERT `reg 99(4B) — a period of one month beginning on this day is allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 12 31) EMPTY

-- Paragraph (4C): a month beginning on 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `reg 99(4C) — a period of one month under paragraph (4A) is running` TRUE TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `reg 99(4C) — a period of one month under paragraph (4A) is running` TRUE TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4C) — a period of one month under paragraph (4A) is running` TRUE TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4C) — a period of one month under paragraph (4A) is running` TRUE TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4C) — a period of one month under paragraph (4A) is running` FALSE TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4C) — a period of one month under paragraph (4A) is running` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15))
-- No date has been specified: no period is running.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(4C) — a period of one month under paragraph (4A) is running` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph (5)(a): a work preparation requirement, or voluntary work preparation as defined in regulation 95(4).
#ASSERT `reg 99(5)(a) — the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement or voluntary work preparation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(5)(a) — the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement or voluntary work preparation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- An action specified as a work preparation requirement is not voluntary work preparation.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5)(a) — the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement or voluntary work preparation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5)(a) — the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement or voluntary work preparation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5)(a) — the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement or voluntary work preparation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- Paragraph (5)(b).
#ASSERT `reg 99(5)(b) — the claimant has temporary child care responsibilities or is dealing with a temporary matter` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(5)(b) — the claimant has temporary child care responsibilities or is dealing with a temporary matter` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5)(b) — the claimant has temporary child care responsibilities or is dealing with a temporary matter` FALSE FALSE)

-- Paragraph (5)(c): unfit for longer than 14 days or for more than 2 periods, and the statement if requested.
#ASSERT `reg 99(5)(c) — the claimant is unfit for work for longer or for more periods than paragraph (4)(a) allows` (`test — unfit` 15 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(5)(c) — the claimant is unfit for work for longer or for more periods than paragraph (4)(a) allows` (`test — unfit` 10 3 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(5)(c) — the claimant is unfit for work for longer or for more periods than paragraph (4)(a) allows` (`test — unfit` 15 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5)(c) — the claimant is unfit for work for longer or for more periods than paragraph (4)(a) allows` (`test — unfit` 15 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5)(c) — the claimant is unfit for work for longer or for more periods than paragraph (4)(a) allows` (`test — unfit` 14 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))

-- Paragraph (5)(d): paragraph (4) would apply but for paragraph (4ZA).
#ASSERT `reg 99(5)(d) — paragraph (4) would apply but for paragraph (4ZA)` `test — a short absence` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5)(d) — paragraph (4) would apply but for paragraph (4ZA)` `test — a short absence` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5)(d) — paragraph (4) would apply but for paragraph (4ZA)` `test — a short absence` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5)(d) — paragraph (4) would apply but for paragraph (4ZA)` (`test — unfit` 15 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE FALSE)

-- The four sub-paragraphs, then paragraphs (5), (5A) and (5B).
#ASSERT `reg 99(5) — the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(5) — the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(5) — the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(5) — the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5) — the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(5) — this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5) — this paragraph applies` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5) — this paragraph applies` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(5A) — this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5A) — this paragraph applies` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5A) — this paragraph applies` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(5B) — this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5B) — this paragraph applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5B) — this paragraph applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(5B) — this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph (6)(a): 18 hours at 10 pounds an hour is 18 x 10 x 52 / 12 = 780.
#ASSERT `reg 99(6)(a) — the claimant's monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 18 hours` 780 10
#ASSERT `reg 99(6)(a) — the claimant's monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 18 hours` 1000 10
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(6)(a) — the claimant's monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 18 hours` 779.99 10)
-- At 11.44 an hour: 18 x 11.44 x 52 / 12 = 892.32, and regulation 6(1A) disregards the fraction: 892.
#ASSERT `reg 99(6)(a) — the claimant's monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 18 hours` 892 11.44
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(6)(a) — the claimant's monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 18 hours` 891.99 11.44)

-- Paragraph (6)(b): 29 hours at 10 pounds an hour is 29 x 10 x 52 / 12 = 1256.66..., truncated to 1256.
#ASSERT `reg 99(6)(b) — the couple's combined monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 29 hours` `joint claimants` 1256 10
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(6)(b) — the couple's combined monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 29 hours` `joint claimants` 1255.99 10)
#ASSERT `reg 99(6)(b) — the couple's combined monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 29 hours` `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` 2000 10
-- A single claimant who is not a member of a couple has no couple.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(6)(b) — the couple's combined monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 29 hours` `a single claimant` 5000 10)
#ASSERT `reg 99(6) — this paragraph applies` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(6) — this paragraph applies` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(6) — this paragraph applies` FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph (1)(a): paragraphs (3), (4), (4A) and (6).
#ASSERT `reg 99(1)(a) — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(1)(a) — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(1)(a) — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(1)(a) — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(1)(a) — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- Paragraph (1)(b): the meaning of "able and willing immediately to take up work"; NOTHING when none of the paragraphs applies.
#ASSERT `reg 99(1)(b) — the claimant is able and willing immediately to take up work` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 99(1)(b) — the claimant is able and willing immediately to take up work` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(1)(b) — the claimant is able and willing immediately to take up work` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Paragraph (2): a work search requirement ceases to have effect from the date the circumstances begin (1 March 2026).
#ASSERT `reg 99(2) — a work search requirement previously applying has ceased to have effect` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `reg 99(2) — a work search requirement previously applying has ceased to have effect` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(2) — a work search requirement previously applying has ceased to have effect` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(2) — a work search requirement previously applying has ceased to have effect` NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1))

-- Paragraph (2A).
#ASSERT `reg 99(2A)(a) — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(2A)(a) — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 99(2A)(b) — a work search requirement previously applying has ceased to have effect` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(2A)(b) — a work search requirement previously applying has ceased to have effect` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99(2A)(b) — a work search requirement previously applying has ceased to have effect` NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1))

-- Paragraph (2B) and (2C).
#ASSERT `reg 99(2B) — the claimant is able and willing to take up work` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 99(2B) — the claimant is able and willing to take up work` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(2B) — the claimant is able and willing to take up work` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 99(2C) — the claimant is able and willing to take up work` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 99(2C) — the claimant is able and willing to take up work` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(2C) — the claimant is able and willing to take up work` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99(2C) — the claimant is able and willing to take up work` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The composite: paragraphs (3), (4), (4A), (5) and (6), in that order of arguments.
#ASSERT `reg 99 — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99 — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 99 — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 99 — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
